From: StickOS <dev@pinux.xyz>
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: no connector ID interrupt on host-only ports

On the RK3066 left running by the stock kernel, the host-only port (dr_mode = "host")
gets a connector ID status change interrupt at every core init; the handler inits the
core again, so it never stops. The ID pin matters only to ports that can change role.

---
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/hcd.c
@@ -54,7 +54,8 @@
 
 	if (!hsotg->params.host_dma)
 		intmsk |= GINTSTS_RXFLVL;
-	if (!hsotg->params.external_id_pin_ctl)
+	/* the ID pin matters only to ports that can change role */
+	if (!hsotg->params.external_id_pin_ctl && hsotg->dr_mode == USB_DR_MODE_OTG)
 		intmsk |= GINTSTS_CONIDSTSCHNG;
 
 	intmsk |= GINTSTS_WKUPINT | GINTSTS_USBSUSP |
